wayland-protocols: Build the fallback's enum headers with an older wayland-scanner

Mesa 26.3.0-rc3 needs wayland-protocols 1.49 (347b5c45fd2). Where the
system's is older, as Debian 13's 1.44, meson builds Mesa's
wayland-protocols subproject, which makes its enum headers with
"wayland-scanner --strict". The 1.49 protocols use the "frozen" attribute
of wayland-scanner 1.24's DTD, so the strict validation of Debian 13's
1.23.1 fails the D3D12 OpenGL build; Mesa does not use those headers.
Drop --strict from them, through the wrap's diff_files. Systems with
wayland-protocols 1.49 (Fedora 44, Arch) do not use the subproject. Drop it
when the hosts' wayland-scanner is 1.24 or newer.

diff --git a/subprojects/packagefiles/wayland-protocols-scanner-1.23.patch b/subprojects/packagefiles/wayland-protocols-scanner-1.23.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0d635f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/subprojects/packagefiles/wayland-protocols-scanner-1.23.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+--- a/include/wayland-protocols/meson.build
++++ b/include/wayland-protocols/meson.build
+@@ -7,7 +7,6 @@
+ 		input: '../..' / protocol_file,
+ 		command: [
+ 			prog_scanner,
+-			'--strict',
+ 			'enum-header',
+ 			'@INPUT@',
+ 			'@OUTPUT@',
diff --git a/subprojects/wayland-protocols.wrap b/subprojects/wayland-protocols.wrap
index 9ccac39..12aba79 100644
--- a/subprojects/wayland-protocols.wrap
+++ b/subprojects/wayland-protocols.wrap
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ directory = wayland-protocols-1.49
 source_url = https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/releases/1.49/downloads/wayland-protocols-1.49.tar.xz
 source_filename = wayland-protocols-1.49.tar.xz
 source_hash = ec4c8f74942d6dff7ace8b4ce4764f0ef9ff618a935d974ea77edee2ad240b14
+diff_files = wayland-protocols-scanner-1.23.patch
 
 [provide]
 wayland-protocols = wayland_protocols
